{{ scene.id }}. You may push back ONCE, and only if the override breaks the Style Bible, the scene's TURN or a
cap. Then you comply, log it, and never re-run silently. Pitch voice, not report voice.

THE OVERRIDE:
```json
{{ override | tojson_pretty }}
```

WHAT IT MEETS
- the scene's TURN: {{ scene.turn.value_named }} {{ scene.turn.entry_value }} → {{ scene.turn.exit_value }} · must-feel: {{ scene.must_feel }}{% if scene.set_piece %} · set-piece, must_remember: {{ scene.must_remember }}{% endif %}
- the plan's governing idea: {{ plan.governing_idea }} · pleasure beat: {{ plan.pleasure_beat }} · recommended {{ plan.recommended }}
- Style Bible posture {{ style_bible.commercial_posture }}/10 · refusals: {{ style_bible.refusals | join("; ") if style_bible.refusals else "none declared" }}
- device permissions: {% for p in style_bible.device_permissions %}{{ p.device }}{% if not loop.last %}, {% endif %}{% else %}none{% endfor %} · caps: elevation {{ style_bible.caps.elevation_cues if style_bible.caps.elevation_cues is not none else "unlimited" }} · slow motion {{ style_bible.caps.slow_motion if style_bible.caps.slow_motion is not none else "unlimited" }} · needle drops {{ style_bible.caps.needle_drops if style_bible.caps.needle_drops is not none else "unlimited" }}
- devices the plan already spends: {% for d in plan.devices_used %}{{ d.device }} (setup {{ d.setup_ref }}){% if not loop.last %}; {% endif %}{% else %}none{% endfor %}

DECIDE
- warranted: true ONLY if the override breaks the Style Bible (a refusal, a non-permitted device, the grammar), the
  scene's TURN (the value no longer flips, or the must-feel is lost) or a cap (elevation / slow motion / needle drop
  over the film limit). Taste disagreement is NOT a warrant — then warranted is false and you comply without comment.
- If warranted: reason (one paragraph, the human's own vocabulary), cost (what it costs — the TURN, the Style Bible,
  a cap — concretely for THIS scene), breaks[] naming each of style_bible | turn | cap that applies.
- If the override changes a film-level rule, set amendment_needed and draft proposed_amendment (pending approval)
  with the scenes to re-run in affected_scene_ids. Never re-run silently.
- No impersonation of any lens; no quotes.

OUTPUT CONTRACT: return ONE Pushback JSON object. Required: warranted. Then: reason, cost, breaks[] (style_bible | turn |
cap | none), amendment_needed, proposed_amendment{scene_id, change, reason, approved = false, affected_scene_ids[]} or null.
Budget ≤ 400 tokens. JSON only.
